# ============================================================================
# Herald Demo Test - Third-Party Credentials
#
# Copy this file to .env.demo and fill in real values.
# .env.demo is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
#
# When credentials are absent, live tests (demo/e2e/live/) are automatically
# skipped so that other demo tests still run normally.
#
# NOTE: The demo seed (scripts/lib/demo_seed.py) NO LONGER seeds placeholder
# entitlement mappings. The Stripe/Creem catalog is pulled via provider sync
# from the UI (or by tests) against the real products configured here. To
# populate the /manage/billing/entitlement-mappings page, log in as admin and
# click "Sync" after starting the demo.
# ============================================================================

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub OAuth (per-realm, injected via API during test setup)
#
# How to get these values:
#   1. Go to https://github.com/settings/developers
#   2. Click "New OAuth App" (or "New GitHub App")
#   3. Fill in:
#      - Application name:  Herald Demo
#      - Homepage URL:      http://localhost:3000
#      - Authorization callback URL:
#          http://localhost:8080/api/oauth/{realmId}/github/callback
#          (replace {realmId} with your realm, e.g. "admin")
#   4. After creation, click "Generate a new client secret"
#   5. Copy "Client ID" → GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
#      Copy "Client Secret" → GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Creem Payment (per-realm, injected via API during test setup)
#
# How to get these values:
#   1. Create a merchant account at https://creem.io (invite-only)
#   2. In the Creem Dashboard:
#      a. API Key:
#         - Go to Developers → API Keys
#         - Copy the API key (starts with "ck_test_" in test mode)
#         - Paste → CREEM_API_KEY
#      b. Webhook Secret:
#         - Go to Developers → Webhooks
#         - Click "Create Webhook"
#         - Name: Herald Demo
#         - URL: http://localhost:8080/api/third/pay/{realmId}/creem/webhooks
#           (replace {realmId} with your realm, e.g. "admin")
#         - Select events: checkout.completed, subscription.active,
#           subscription.paid, subscription.canceled, refund.created
#         - After creation, copy the "Signing secret"
#         - Paste → CREEM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   3. Products (optional — live test creates them automatically):
#      - The live test uses fixed identifiers:
#        • Product name: herald-live-creem-product
#        • Plan name:    herald-live-creem-plan
#      - If you want to pre-create them in Creem Dashboard:
#        Go to Products → Create Product → use the names above
#
# Test mode:
#   - Use test API key (ck_test_*) for development
#   - Test card: 4242 4242 4242 4242, any future expiry, any CVC
#   - Test API base: https://test-api.creem.io
#   - Production API base: https://api.creem.io
#
# Ref: https://docs.creem.io/getting-started/quickstart
# Ref: https://docs.creem.io/skills/creem-api/WEBHOOKS
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREEM_API_KEY=
CREEM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
CREEM_PRODUCT_ID=prod_xxxxx

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe Payment (per-realm, injected via API during test setup)
#
# How to get these values:
#   1. Create an account at https://dashboard.stripe.com/register
#   2. Switch to "Test mode" (toggle in top-right corner)
#   3. In the Stripe Dashboard:
#      a. Publishable Key & Secret Key:
#         - Go to Developers → API Keys
#         - Copy "Publishable key" (starts with "pk_test_") → STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#         - Copy "Secret key" (starts with "sk_test_") → STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
#           (click "Reveal test key" if masked)
#      b. Product:
#         - Go to Products → Add product
#         - Name: Herald Live Stripe Product
#         - Price: Recurring, $10.00/month
#         - After creation, copy the Product ID (starts with "prod_")
#         - Paste → STRIPE_PRODUCT_ID
#      c. Webhook Secret:
#         - Go to Developers → Webhooks
#         - Click "Add endpoint"
#         - Endpoint URL: https://{ngrok-domain}/api/third/pay/{realmId}/stripe/webhooks
#           (replace {realmId} with your realm, e.g. "admin")
#         - Select events: checkout.session.completed
#         - After creation, click "Reveal" under "Signing secret"
#         - Copy the value (starts with "whsec_") → STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#
# Test mode:
#   - Test card: 4242 4242 4242 4242, expiry 12/34, CVC 123
#   - Use test API keys (pk_test_*/sk_test_*) for development
#
# Ref: https://docs.stripe.com/keys
# Ref: https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRODUCT_ID=prod_xxxxx

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ngrok Tunnel (exposes localhost:8080 for third-party callbacks)
#
# Setup:
#   1. Sign up at https://dashboard.ngrok.com/signup
#   2. Copy your authtoken from https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken
#      → set as NGROK_AUTHTOKEN
#   3. (Paid plan) Reserve a domain at https://dashboard.ngrok.com/domains
#      → set as NGROK_DOMAIN for a fixed URL
#   4. Start the tunnel:
#      uv run scripts/ngrok-tunnel.py
#   5. Inspector UI: http://localhost:4040
#
# Free plan: ngrok assigns a random URL each time (check console output).
# Paid plan:  set NGROK_DOMAIN for a stable URL (e.g. my-app.ngrok-free.app).
#
# Use the ngrok URL when configuring third-party dashboards:
#   - Creem webhook URL: https://{ngrok-domain}/api/third/pay/{realmId}/creem/webhooks
#   - GitHub OAuth callback: https://{ngrok-domain}/api/oauth/{realmId}/github/callback
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=
NGROK_DOMAIN=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe One-Time Product (for one-time payment invoice live tests)
#
# How to create:
#   1. In Stripe Dashboard (test mode) → Products → Add product
#   2. Name: Herald Live Stripe One-Time Product
#   3. Price: One-time, $5.00 (or any amount)
#   4. Copy the Product ID (prod_*) → STRIPE_ONETIME_PRODUCT_ID
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_ONETIME_PRODUCT_ID=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Creem One-Time Product (for one-time payment invoice live tests)
#
# How to create:
#   1. In Creem Dashboard → Products → Create Product
#   2. Name: herald-live-creem-onetime-product
#   3. Price type: One-time
#   4. Copy the Product ID → CREEM_ONETIME_PRODUCT_ID
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREEM_ONETIME_PRODUCT_ID=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QQ Mail SMTP (per-realm, injected via API during test setup)
#
# Used by: demo/e2e/live/core/us-ra-013-qq-smtp-live.e2e.ts (US-RA-013 场景2,
#          US-RA-014 场景1).
#
# How to get these values:
#   1. Log in to QQ Mail at https://mail.qq.com
#   2. 设置 (Settings) → 账户 (Account)
#   3. Under "POP3/IMAP/SMTP/Exchange/CardDAV/CalDAV Service", enable
#      "IMAP/SMTP Service"
#   4. Click "Generate Authorization Code" (生成授权码). A 16-char string is
#      returned — copy it to QQ_SMTP_PASSWORD. This is NOT your QQ login
#      password.
#
# When QQ_SMTP_HOST/PORT/USERNAME/PASSWORD are unset, the QQ SMTP live test
# is skipped (does not block the rest of the demo suite).
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
QQ_SMTP_HOST=smtp.qq.com
QQ_SMTP_PORT=465
QQ_SMTP_USERNAME=your-qq@qq.com
QQ_SMTP_PASSWORD=
QQ_SMTP_ENCRYPTION=ssl
# Optional — defaults to QQ_SMTP_USERNAME:
QQ_FROM_ADDRESS=
# Optional — test email recipient, defaults to QQ_SMTP_USERNAME:
QQ_TEST_RECIPIENT=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resend Email (admin realm email channel; seeded at demo-start)
#
# How to get these values:
#   1. Sign up at https://resend.com (free tier: 3,000 emails/month,
#      100/day)
#   2. Go to https://resend.com/api-keys → "Create API Key"
#   3. Copy the key (starts with "re_") → RESEND_API_KEY
#   4. (Optional) Verify a sending domain at https://resend.com/domains
#      and set RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS to an address on it, e.g.
#      noreply@yourdomain.com
#
# When RESEND_API_KEY is set, demo-start seeds the admin realm's email
# channel (realm_config config_type='email': provider=resend,
# from_address, resend_api_key) so the realm starts configured. When it is
# absent the rows are NOT seeded and the channel stays unconfigured —
# EmailService::send_email then silently skips instead of failing.
#
# Default sender is onboarding@resend.dev, Resend's shared test address:
# without a verified domain it only delivers to the Resend account owner's
# own mailbox.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to onboarding@resend.dev:
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=
